{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea","id":931143,"title":"Thinking about changing how Breaking Points work, bad idea?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-13T19:34:34-07:00","id":931143,"title":"Thinking about changing how Breaking Points work, bad idea?","content":"Here is the way its written:<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> Dramatic Failure: The character\u2019s worldview has been<br /> damaged, perhaps beyond repair. The character suffers from<br /> traumatic stress. Lose a dot of Integrity and choose from the<br /> following Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller<br /> approval): Broken, Fugue, or Madness. Also, take a Beat.<br /> Failure: The character\u2019s worldview has been shaken and he<br /> probably questions his sense of self, his ability to relate to people,<br /> his own moral worth, or his sanity. Lose a dot of Integrity and<br /> choose one of the following Conditions (or create a new one<br /> with Storyteller approval): Guilty, Shaken, or Spooked.<br /> <b>Success: The character has come through the breaking<br /> point intact. He might feel guilty or upset about what<br /> happened, but he can cope. Choose one of the following<br /> Conditions (or create a new one with Storyteller approval):<br /> Guilty, Shaken, or Spooked. <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><i>&quot;What,Why?&quot;</i></span></b><br /> Exceptional Success: The character somehow manages to<br /> not only survive the breaking point but to also find meaning<br /> in it, to reaffirm his own self-worth, or to pass through fire<br /> and be tempered by it. The character takes a Beat<br /> and regains a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> So if I change this, I want to make it where a success gives no negative conditions, but instead gives a beat. It seems strange to me that Integrity cost 5 EXP per point, considering it really doesn't do a whole lot for you. Am I missing something? Why is it so punishing? Will changing this cause some unforeseen issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","user":"K9ine","date":". 07-13-2016, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T19:59:24-07:00","id":931151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea#post931143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems strange to me that Integrity cost 5 EXP per point</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems strange to me that you're bringing this up in the context of having bolded the text of the Success result.<br /> <br /> Integrity costs three Experiences per dot, Shaken and Spooked are trivial to discharge and their mechanics are literally just &quot;fail a roll and you get a Beat,&quot; and the benefit of a success over a failure on a breaking point roll is that <i>you don't lose Integrity</i>.<br /> <br /> Making the change is not so much a bad idea as it is confusing in its basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:05:54-07:00","id":931152,"title":"","content":"It's basically &quot;think what stopped your character for losing your Integrity, express that using a Condition, and grab a Beat.&quot; A carrot for roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:07:34-07:00","id":931153,"title":"","content":"It's actually more of a positive than not.<br /> <br /> The EXP Economy is, in very generic terms, slanted towards the angle of getting you in and out of trouble and generating moments of tension. THe more you risk Integrity, the fact you improve, as an example. Succeeding at an Integrity Roll preserves your Integrity and gives you an opportunity to gain Beats for generating EXP.<br /> <br /> So, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:07:57-07:00","id":931154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931151#post931151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems strange to me that you're bringing this up in the context of having bolded the text of the Success result.<br /> <br /> Integrity costs three Experiences per dot, Shaken and Spooked are trivial to discharge and their mechanics are literally just &quot;fail a roll and you get a Beat,&quot; and the benefit of a success over a failure on a breaking point roll is that <i>you don't lose Integrity</i>.<br /> <br /> Making the change is not so much a bad idea as it is confusing in its basis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess I misread it, I thought it cost 5. My thinking is that Shaken and Spooked can endanger your character, so the only time Integrity seems to work to your advantage is when you very rarely get an exceptional success. Mortals don't get a supernatural resistance from it, and all it seems to do is give you a minor bonus to resisting breaking points at higher levels. It just doesn't seem like a balanced trait to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:23:46-07:00","id":931162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931154#post931154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I misread it, I thought it cost 5. My thinking is that Shaken and Spooked can endanger your character, so the only time Integrity seems to work to your advantage is when you very rarely get an exceptional success. Mortals don't get a supernatural resistance from it, and all it seems to do is give you a minor bonus to resisting breaking points at higher levels. It just doesn't seem like a balanced trait to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Balanced against what? Supernaturals? Mortals are extremely ill equipped to deal with them. That's a feature, not a bug. It also falls squarely into the player's hands how to resolve their conditions, pick when shaken screws them over, and when spooked causes undue fascination with things best left undisturbed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:34:52-07:00","id":931165,"title":"","content":"If you are uninterested in dynamics of Integrity Economy, and dislike the idea of using XP to buy it back, here is a following hack:<br /> <br /> Instead of 1-10 Integrity scale, you have 3 Integrity Tiers: Tempered, Stable and Unstable.<br /> <br /> While Tempered, Characters roll 5 Dice for Integrity Rolls; while Stable, they roll 3 Dice. When Unstable, they roll 1 Dice. You may use Willpower to affect these, and source of the Breaking Roll may apply bonuses or maluses.<br /> <br /> While Tempered, succeeding on a Integrity Roll gives you Steadfast Condition, and drops you back to Stable. You may become Tempered as a alternative to getting all your Willpower back by fullfiling your Virtue, or by spending a Willpower while succeeding on Integrity Roll while Stable. Failing a Integrity Roll while Tempered drops you back to Stable and gives you a Beat.<br /> <br /> While Stable, succeeding on a Integrity Roll gives you a positive Condition relevant to the situation that restores you 1 Willpower point when resolved, or allows you to spend a Willpower point to become Tempered. Failing Integrity Roll while Stable makes you temporarily Unstable and gives you a negative Condition; you remain Unstable until you resolve it.<br /> <br /> While Unstable, you suffer from a negative Condition - resolving it makes you Stable again. When succeeding on a Integrity Roll while Unstable, you may spend a Willpower point to become Stable again, or gain a small positive Condition that allows you to restore one Willpower point while resolved.<br /> Failing Integrity roll while Unstable gives you a choice - either spend a Willpower point and gain a Beat, or gain another negative Condition attached to Unstability. You need to resolve them both in order to become Stable again, and you may only resolve one of them per Scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just made it up, so it's probably pretty shaky, but it's an alternative to the Integrity system if you are more heroic oriented CofD. Or at least, more action-horror. It also makes Integrity go up and down rapidly during the game, which makes it more interesting if you are looking for short-term &quot;Sanity&quot; mechanic instead of long-term integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T21:17:21-07:00","id":931177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931154#post931154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess I misread it, I thought it cost 5. My thinking is that Shaken and Spooked can endanger your character, so the only time Integrity seems to work to your advantage is when you very rarely get an exceptional success. Mortals don't get a supernatural resistance from it, and all it seems to do is give you a minor bonus to resisting breaking points at higher levels. It just doesn't seem like a balanced trait to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about as balanced as all of the other creatures types of morality bars (Humanity/Harmony/Clarity). It gives a decent way of getting beats and represents the mental state of your character to a limited degree. Why would it affect much?<br /> <br /> Though, it does have some interaction with the supernatural, as it increases the power of abjuration and banishment attempts iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:29:58-07:00","id":931213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931162#post931162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Balanced against what? Supernaturals? Mortals are extremely ill equipped to deal with them. That's a feature, not a bug. It also falls squarely into the player's hands how to resolve their conditions, pick when shaken screws them over, and when spooked causes undue fascination with things best left undisturbed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Balanced aganist itself. It is more negative than positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:37:11-07:00","id":931217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931165#post931165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are uninterested in dynamics of Integrity Economy, and dislike the idea of using XP to buy it back, here is a following hack:<br /> <br /> Instead of 1-10 Integrity scale, you have 3 Integrity Tiers: Tempered, Stable and Unstable.<br /> <br /> While Tempered, Characters roll 5 Dice for Integrity Rolls; while Stable, they roll 3 Dice. When Unstable, they roll 1 Dice. You may use Willpower to affect these, and source of the Breaking Roll may apply bonuses or maluses.<br /> <br /> While Tempered, succeeding on a Integrity Roll gives you Steadfast Condition, and drops you back to Stable. You may become Tempered as a alternative to getting all your Willpower back by fullfiling your Virtue, or by spending a Willpower while succeeding on Integrity Roll while Stable. Failing a Integrity Roll while Tempered drops you back to Stable and gives you a Beat.<br /> <br /> While Stable, succeeding on a Integrity Roll gives you a positive Condition relevant to the situation that restores you 1 Willpower point when resolved, or allows you to spend a Willpower point to become Tempered. Failing Integrity Roll while Stable makes you temporarily Unstable and gives you a negative Condition; you remain Unstable until you resolve it.<br /> <br /> While Unstable, you suffer from a negative Condition - resolving it makes you Stable again. When succeeding on a Integrity Roll while Unstable, you may spend a Willpower point to become Stable again, or gain a small positive Condition that allows you to restore one Willpower point while resolved.<br /> Failing Integrity roll while Unstable gives you a choice - either spend a Willpower point and gain a Beat, or gain another negative Condition attached to Unstability. You need to resolve them both in order to become Stable again, and you may only resolve one of them per Scene.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just made it up, so it's probably pretty shaky, but it's an alternative to the Integrity system if you are more heroic oriented CofD. Or at least, more action-horror. It also makes Integrity go up and down rapidly during the game, which makes it more interesting if you are looking for short-term &quot;Sanity&quot; mechanic instead of long-term integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really think its pretty good. My main consern is that Integrity almost never does anything good for the player. The only time it is useful is when you get a exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T23:40:49-07:00","id":931219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931177#post931177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about as balanced as all of the other creatures types of morality bars (Humanity/Harmony/Clarity). It gives a decent way of getting beats and represents the mental state of your character to a limited degree. Why would it affect much?<br /> <br /> Though, it does have some interaction with the supernatural, as it increases the power of abjuration and banishment attempts iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it just seems like if you made a high integrity character, you should get some sort of special benifit out of it. My storyteller didn't let us use willpower to boost it, The rules never said you could, but we all assumed it was supposed to be unaffected by it, now I can't remember why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T00:12:53-07:00","id":931225,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is like complaining that the Sanity stat in Call of Cthulhu doesn't benefit your character. It's not really there to be a thing that benefits you. It represents how well your character deals with trauma. Being really good at dealing with trauma doesn't really have any special benefits beyond making you less likely to be severely impacted by traumatic events. Traumatic events themselves are very rarely a good thing. In some rare cases (exceptional success), you can learn and grow from them. This is more likely when you are especially good at coping with trauma (when you have high Integrity), but most of the time, most people are just thankful if a traumatic event leaves them briefly rattled (guilty/shaken/spooked) and that's it.<br /> <br /> Also, a successful Breaking Point roll <i>does</i> benefit you. By giving you a Beat. Sure, you have to fail a roll, or pursue something that might be dangerous, or confess to having done the traumatic thing to get that Beat, but that's how Beats are obtained more often than not. That's a big part of character advancement in CofD 2e, you gain experience is by putting your character at risk to heighten the drama. Gulty, Shaken, and Spooked are all extremely low-risk as far as Conditions go. In this way, succeeding a Breaking Point roll successfully models a realistic response to trauma, escalates the dramatic tension in the story, <i>and</i> rewards you with character advancement bennies all in one go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-14-2016, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T05:12:27-07:00","id":931279,"title":"","content":"High integrity does help, namely in that you are less likely to come crashing down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T05:18:05-07:00","id":931281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931219#post931219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it just seems like if you made a high integrity character, you should get some sort of special benifit out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do, you're less likely to break down and you deal with trauma better, and it makes you better at fighting ephemeral creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:43:32-07:00","id":931455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931279#post931279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High integrity does help, namely in that you are less likely to come crashing down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you get actual bonus to those rolls if your integrity is past a certain level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:47:33-07:00","id":931458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931455#post931455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you get actual bonus to those rolls if your integrity is past a certain level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T10:58:39-07:00","id":931464,"title":"","content":"On breaking points, nothing else as far as I have read. I wouldn't really have a problem so much with this if a success on a breaking point gave you good conditions instead of bad, or simply gave you no condition but and extra beat. Do know if Willpower can boost breaking points? I would have thought no, because it seems like a passive thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:06:57-07:00","id":931504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931464#post931464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On breaking points, nothing else as far as I have read.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also gives a bonus to Abjuration rolls (see page 140), and gives the storyteller a smaller dice pool to use against you with the Madness Condition (see page 289). And I guess you've got a better resistance against Lunacy, since Lunacy is a special Breaking Point roll. But yeah, most of what high Integrity is good for is keeping you from losing more Integrity. Just like high Sanity in Call of Cthulhu and other games that borrow the mechanic is mostly just good for keeping you from losing more Sanity. That's why I made that comparison in the first place. Think about it like a sort of health track, having high health is its own reward, because it makes it harder for you to run out of health. You don't need bonuses for having high HP or rewards for successful dodge rolls (beyond, you know, not losing HP), but you don't call health an &quot;unbalanced mechanic&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931464#post931464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't really have a problem so much with this if a success on a breaking point gave you good conditions instead of bad, or simply gave you no condition but and extra beat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you get a beneficial Condition for that. You were still just exposed to something horrific, and a success only means you're able to cope with what you experienced without suffering long-term psychological harm. The benefit from succeeding a Breaking Point roll is <i>not losing Integrity</i>. Actually coming out of such an experience more resolved is an exceptional thing, which means it requires exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931464#post931464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do know if Willpower can boost breaking points? I would have thought no, because it seems like a passive thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know of any reason you wouldn't be able to spend Willpower on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T19:15:12-07:00","id":931753,"title":"","content":"High Integrity makes you one badass cabr\u00f3n when it comes to exorcisms and the like.<br /> <br /> Someone with high Integrity (let's say Integrity 8) and a decent Resolve/Composure (we're talking 3 dots each) who has a Virtue of &quot;Thorough&quot; can kill someone in cold blood without suffering Integrity loss. We're talking &quot;I'm rolling 4 dice. Yes, that's <i>after</i> the -5 penalty.&quot; Heck, if you have the right Conditions (Inspired, maybe?), that murder can <i>reinforce your sense of self</i>.<br /> <br /> Same guy could run a good Abjuration - 9 dice vs. the Ephemeral Being's Power + Resistance is <i>pretty solid</i> against low-grade Ephemeral Being. Checking 2nd Edition Core, they'd have a pretty even chance against pretty much all of the Rank 1 or 2 Angels. Toss on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1jM_bpQHo-dM4yop592S09y4AjQGLLTNhK5_0-5_85kg/edit#heading=h.4nug3g6xq3z9\" target=\"_blank\">Hardened Exorcist</a>, and you've got a <i>much</i> better dice pool than most of them, and probably a decent dicepool for Warding/Binding as well.<br /> <br /> Hell<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> I like the Integrity replacement, WHW - it got the first Like out of me of this year.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> As for why people don't want it to be a positive Condition, K9ine... some people (silly people!) pretend these are horror games ;p. More seriously, the Conditions it gives you currently pushes you towards making <i>more</i> Breaking Point rolls, which gives you more delicious XP. And despite the <i>awesome</i> benefits of high Integrity, it's also something that's optional to care about.<br /> <br /> 1) Taking Breaking Point rolls is <i>optional</i>, as long as you have a justification (&quot;My character works at a slaughterhouse - screams stopped bothering me after the first month&quot;).<br /> 2) The Tolerance for Biology merit not only stops you from throwing up at the still-living person turned into Modern Art, it also technically waives any Breaking Point roll involved. Same thing for Raised by Wolves (if you're Wolf-Blooded), except that one also waives Breaking Point rolls for observing the supernatural.<br /> 3) Losing Integrity is actually... not all that bad. Someone at Integrity 1 has a -2 penalty to Breaking Point rolls... if you pick up a meditation habit (Meditative Mind \u2022\u2022), you've counteracted that penalty <i>entirely</i>. So if Example Guy lost 7 dots of Integrity <i>somehow</i>, he'd still have the same dice-pool for murder (he'd lose a die if he does it more than once per day, but <i>still</i>.)<br /> 4) On a meta level, Spooked and Shaken <i>are</i> good Conditions - they give you spotlight time. Guilty is better - it's only really a penalty if your ST calls for a lot of very specific opposed rolls - too bad the example dice pools for those actions are <i>resisted</i>, not <i>opposed</i>. And it lets you ham it up with confessions of guilt - <i>no downsides</i>.<br /> <br /> (On a side note, I kinda want to scrape together a little &quot;handbook&quot; for people who want to play mortal exorcists who punch above their pay grade.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"htt