you ham it up with confessions of guilt - <i>no downsides</i>.<br /> <br /> (On a side note, I kinda want to scrape together a little &quot;handbook&quot; for people who want to play mortal exorcists who punch above their pay grade.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So much misleading and glossed over stuff, I'll get back to this later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T10:03:36-07:00","id":932068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931910#post931910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So much misleading and glossed over stuff, I'll get back to this later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you do so quickly? I don't appreciate being called a liar by someone who doesn't supply a reason.<br /> <br /> I mean, by all means - correct me if I'm wrong. I just find it kinda insulting the way you're going about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T14:42:36-07:00","id":932220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931455#post931455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't you get actual bonus to those rolls if your integrity is past a certain level?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine this has been answered already, but yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T16:24:17-07:00","id":932247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=931753#post931753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why people don't want it to be a positive Condition, K9ine... some people (silly people!) pretend these are horror games ;p. More seriously, the Conditions it gives you currently pushes you towards making <i>more</i> Breaking Point rolls, which gives you more delicious XP. And despite the <i>awesome</i> benefits of high Integrity, it's also something that's optional to care about.<br /> <br /> 1) Taking Breaking Point rolls is <i>optional</i>, as long as you have a justification (&quot;My character works at a slaughterhouse - screams stopped bothering me after the first month&quot;).<br /> 2) The Tolerance for Biology merit not only stops you from throwing up at the still-living person turned into Modern Art, it also technically waives any Breaking Point roll involved. Same thing for Raised by Wolves (if you're Wolf-Blooded), except that one also waives Breaking Point rolls for observing the supernatural.<br /> 3) Losing Integrity is actually... not all that bad. Someone at Integrity 1 has a -2 penalty to Breaking Point rolls... if you pick up a meditation habit (Meditative Mind \u2022\u2022), you've counteracted that penalty <i>entirely</i>. So if Example Guy lost 7 dots of Integrity <i>somehow</i>, he'd still have the same dice-pool for murder (he'd lose a die if he does it more than once per day, but <i>still</i>.)<br /> 4) On a meta level, Spooked and Shaken <i>are</i> good Conditions - they give you spotlight time. Guilty is better - it's only really a penalty if your ST calls for a lot of very specific opposed rolls - too bad the example dice pools for those actions are <i>resisted</i>, not <i>opposed</i>. And it lets you ham it up with confessions of guilt - <i>no downsides</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't my intention to come off as calling you a liar.<br /> <br /> 1) Tolerance for Biology reads:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:EscalidoGothico\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\"><span style=\"font-family:EscalidoGothico\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">You do not need to make Composure, Stamina, or Resolve rolls to withstand the biologically strange. <b>This doesn\u2019t mean she\u2019s </b><b>immune to fear; she\u2019s just used to nature in all its nasty forms.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Being used to something doesn't means you don't suffer from it, you won't be having breaking points at the sight of blood, but some creature cutting open someone like they're a bag of Cherios will have a tool in your psychic. Soldiers involved in combat again and again still wind up in unpleasant statistics. Cops still need counsel after every shootout. Killing people is always a breaking point. Etc.<br /> <br /> 2) Not everything supernatural. The mystical strange. The bizarre. Some spirit hitching a ride on your body and urging you to helplessly kill your kid will fuck you up still. Because if you were urged you had it in you in the first place. That's the worst part.<br /> <br /> 3) You're still on the verge of becoming hopelessly (unplayably) insane.<br /> <br /> 4) Agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T16:55:58-07:00","id":932253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=932247#post932247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't my intention to come off as calling you a liar.<br /> <br /> 1) Tolerance for Biology reads:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:EscalidoGothico\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\"><span style=\"font-family:EscalidoGothico\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial-Black\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Bold\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">You do not need to make Composure, Stamina, or Resolve rolls to withstand the biologically strange. <b>This doesn\u2019t mean she\u2019s </b><b>immune to fear; she\u2019s just used to nature in all its nasty forms.</b></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> Being used to something doesn't means you don't suffer from it, you won't be having breaking points at the sight of blood, but some creature cutting open someone like they're a bag of Cherios will have a tool in your psychic. Soldiers involved in combat again and again still wind up in unpleasant statistics. Cops still need counsel after every shootout. Killing people is always a breaking point. Etc.<br /> <br /> 2) Not everything supernatural. The mystical strange. The bizarre. Some spirit hitching a ride on your body and urging you to helplessly kill your kid will fuck you up still. Because if you were urged you had it in you in the first place. That's the worst part.<br /> <br /> 3) You're still on the verge of becoming hopelessly (unplayably) insane.<br /> <br /> 4) Agreed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firefox crashed when I was nearly done with a big post, so let's try something shorter.<br /> <br /> 1 + 2) I never said you were immune to <i>all</i> of them, did I? I pretty much meant what you're arguing. Similarly, you don't get Breaking Points for seeing someone explode into a swarm of rats... but you'd still take it right to the proverbial crotch if you murder your kid due to urging (which you should have thrown off - you have a choice, you know.)<br /> <br /> 3) You can't fall any further and you aren't going to have Dramatic Failures unless you choose to. You're just going to have Shaken/Spooked/Guilty more often. Which we have established is a <i>good</i> idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:13:28-07:00","id":932260,"title":"","content":"I haven't played in actual Integrity game for a very long time, but isn't there a point where low Integrity character can get enough penalties to Integrity roll so they fall into a Chance Die territory for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:25:50-07:00","id":932264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=932260#post932260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't played in actual Integrity game for a very long time, but isn't there a point where low Integrity character can get enough penalties to Integrity roll so they fall into a Chance Die territory for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if you didn't put points in Resolve or Composure. Which, given how <i>good</i> they are and how appropriate they are for most long term-characters, makes me question why.<br /> <br /> Basically, if you have Resolve 3 and Composure 3 and Integrity 1, you're looking at a 4-die pool as your base. You have a Chance Die only for really heinous stuff. And if you picked up a meditation habit/turned to religion/joined a support group, you can bring it to the point where you <i>never</i> have a Chance Die, no matter how bad the breaking point is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:31:51-07:00","id":932268,"title":"","content":"Yeah, most heinous stuff would put you at -1, which is also easy to fix with Willpower roll. Hmmm. Hmmmmmmmm. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:36:31-07:00","id":932269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=932253#post932253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 + 2) I never said you were immune to <i>all</i> of them, did I?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stating &quot;You're immune to X&quot; is a blanket term, usually. Forgive the misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=932253#post932253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) You can't fall any further and you aren't going to have Dramatic Failures unless you choose to. You're just going to have Shaken/Spooked/Guilty more often. Which we have established is a <i>good</i> idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you become unplayable once your ability to cope with how the world works becomes literally zero? That's my point. You seem to be working under the assumption you can keep playing as if there wasn't any side effect of Integrity zero beyond dice-pool penalties to a roll that would determinate if some stat is deduced, when it's been completely depleted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T17:42:04-07:00","id":932272,"title":"","content":"Can you even fall to 0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T18:07:11-07:00","id":932287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=932272#post932272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you even fall to 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can still roll breaking points at 1, signs point to yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T18:38:23-07:00","id":932304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931143-thinking-about-changing-how-breaking-points-work-bad-idea?p=932287#post932287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can still roll breaking points at 1, signs point to yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you can't. Integrity goes from 1 to 10. Otherwise, Soul Loss would drop you to Integrity 0 instead of stopping at 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T18:42:47-07:00","id":932308,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's a bit confusing, and as far as I know developers haven't really said either way. <br /> <br /> There's no mention of you losing your character sheet due to low Integrity. The rules would suggest that at Integrity 1, you hit a Breaking Point, go through the usual motions of getting a Condition, but then stay at Integrity 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T03:12:39-07:00","id":932458,"title":"","content":"You get the condition because &quot;Breaking Point&quot; is a fancy word for &quot;you've seen or done something that was traumatic to you on a new level. Be freaked out.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you don't like the cost, do what I do: give them opportunities for breaking points upwards, like seeing a psychologist or priest, so they can recoup something lost through typical gameplay through typical gameplay.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I find that, more often than not, I forego rolls and just run Morality/Integrity thematically. Harmony 7 Werewolf just ripped a man in half to protect the pack's duty to the spirit? Congrats: you just realized what it means to be Uratha. Harmony 3 Werewolf just had a set of epiphanies about the value and worth of humanity and human families, becoming more inclined to fight for them? Good job: you're more in touch with your human side. I find that works better because it leaves room to discuss what's happened with players, giving them more control over their characters, and most of them actually enjoy playing up the breaking point to show just how much their character has been mentally damaged.<br /> <br /> I had a character (in a pre-GMC space campaign) have to shoot the ship's former science officer in the back of the head and toss the body into a star to stop him from releasing a dangerous parasite on the galaxy, and basically played her as &quot;renegade shepherd&quot; until the other characters finding out counted as resolution. We didn't roll on it, we just did it. More recently, I had Jean (my French Dragon) take an automatic breaking point when a group of his coworkers were murdered while he wasn't there, with the concession that &quot;he'll win this back when he starts killing people, and that's gonna happen reeeeaaaal soon.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's a fun story to play out. It makes for good narrative and good gameplay. The dice / experience systems are just there to keep us honest: don't let them get in the way of entertaining gameplay and intellectual value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}